  "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#semiotic_projection_1",
  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the visual representation of the woman in a sexualized context",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual material of the woman (VisualMaterial entity: woman) as the embodiment of the act of masturbation referenced in the text. The meme implies that the viewer (user) should identify with or project themselves onto the woman's body as the example of female masturbation, even though the text explicitly states 'it's not just for men'. This projection is reinforced by the visual focus on her body and the explicit textual message, creating a semiotic link where the user is invited to see the woman as the representative of the concept being discussed. The projection is not explicit with deictic pronouns like 'you' or 'me', but it is implicit through the visual and textual framing that positions the woman as the subject of the message and the user as the implied observer or participant in the discourse.",
  "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface",
